  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 200 PM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nThe overall pattern is revealed by a peek at WV imagery. The\ndeep nor'easter sliding up the East Coast is the eastern piece \nof a omega pattern in the H5 flow. The pattern's western trof \nhas a shortwave rounding its nadir. It's pushing into eastern \nKansas and producing some showers that have just snuck into far \nsoutheastern portions of the OAX CWA. \n\nAt the surface, we've spent the day mostly without the benefit\nof sunshine. Temps have lingered in the 60s with a few 70s \ndeveloping mid-day as ceilings have begun to lift and some \nbreaks in the clouds could be appreciated over the southern \nportions of the area.\n\nHave reduced PoPs today with 20-40% chances redeveloping this \nevening with best chances (50-60%) for areas north of \nOmaha/Fremont around 9/10pm. QPF should remain on the light \nside. \n\nOvernight, winds become light and variable along a weak boundary\npushing through the area, especially for the northwestern half \nof the area where winds are slowest. Fog development looks like \na certainty with ample low level moisture. Expect to see some \nvisibility observations to slip below a mile at times. This\nmoisture/fog talk will become a familiar refrain over the next\nweek to be sure.",
